    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-02T09:18:20+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T09:18:20+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T23:48:20Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T23:48:20Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and a cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough will move over SA during the day followed by a cold front early Saturday. Another high pressure ridge will move across during Sunday ahead of a low pressure system expected to develop in the far west later in the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers south of Yunta from the late morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the late afternoon then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 23 to 35.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 32.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Yunta. High chance of showers south of Yunta, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds easterly 20 to 30 km/h shifting north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h during the morning then decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers south of Leigh Creek in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Leigh Creek in the morning. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
